WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-I love having you here.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:04.000
Hey, congrats, by the way, on the new logo here.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.267
-Thank you so much. -Look at this right there.

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.234
That's -- -Clean. Clean.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:10.033
Yes. Yeah, we wanted to go with --

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.701
I mean, ever since, you know, "Fortnite" when we blew up --

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.467
And even when I was younger, I loved doing my hair,

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:15.968
like, a little bit different.

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:18.000
-Yeah. -Bangs down and the rest up.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.667
-It's perfect. -So, yeah, we wanted something

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.100
a little cleaner, a little more professional.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.901
And, dude, yeah, there it is, man.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.834
-Last time you were on our show, you said,

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.100
"Hey, look for me on the big screen

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.801
and the small screen." -Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.934
-I was like, "Okay." You didn't tell me what it was.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.968
But there you are in "Free Guy" with Ryan Reynolds.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.133
I go, "There you go. That's the big screen right there."

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:37.801
-Of all the man crushes, man. I mean, dude, what a stud.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.567
You know what I mean? I mean, wow.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.834
-Wow. Really? -Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.834
You know, when we -- I remember we went to film

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.634
and he walked across the -- the street,

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.334
because they were able to close down

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:48.934
an entire street of an actual city

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.334
to film what we were there for.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.601
And he, like -- like, pointed at me,

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.334
and, like, just started walking across

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.200
and, like, gave me and Jess a huge hug.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.200
-And you were like, "That's Ryan Reynolds."

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.634
-I was...

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.601
-Oh, my God. -"Happy to be here."

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.934
And he's like, "Thank you so much for doing this

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.367
and for being on -- in this film."

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.234
And I was just like -- -Did they want you to act

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.934
from the beginning, or do they want --

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.767
Like, "Hey, teach us how to do all of it."

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.567
-They wanted -- It was more so they wanted me

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.267
to be in it and -- Dude, like, I'm telling you.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.701
I read the script. I was a part of it.

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.434
And I was like, "You guys don't really need help

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.968
with the lingo and everything like that."

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:21.300
They kind of nailed it. -They did?

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.734
-Yeah... -Because I remember I --

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:25.868
I asked you for advice for -- -You never take it, though.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.100
[ Laughter ] -No, but I did take it.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.167
I just didn't -- I didn't do anything with it.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.901
-Right. -But I have -- But I have --

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.701
I took your advice and I have all the things.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:36.000
I have the headset. And you hooked me up. Yeah.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.667
I'm kinda -- I'm set up and ready to go.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.601
-Are you just, like, the best at everything now?

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:41.968
-No, I'm terrible at everything. I'm still bad.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.934
I'm still bad at everything, but I'm like --

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.968
I wanted to pick one thing and get good at it,

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:47.534
and then I just can't do that.

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:49.868
I just play everything poorly.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:51.701
But I have fun. -Well, that's all that matters.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.200
You know what I mean? -No, it's not.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.767
But, dude, look -- -You're a pro gamer.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.501
You crush me at everything.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:58.934
-Low-key, it's all that matters.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.400
I mean, listen, I still get super frustrated when --

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.100
when, you know, Jess and my brothers beat me

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.100
at "Mario Kart" and, like, "Mario Party."

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.501
-Oh. "Mario Party." No, no, no.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:09.934
-Do you have any of the random stars?

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.868
You know what I'm talking about? At the end? The random stars?

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.334
"Oh, you traveled the least amount of spaces.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.000
Here's your star." -No. No.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.534
-And I -- -Yeah. No, no, no.

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:18.934
-How does that work? -No, no, no.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.434
-You can't practice for that, Jimmy.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:21.834
-Oh, no. I don't -- Yeah.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.434
I thought you were talking about when people steal your star.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.367
-Oh, people steal your stars. -"We're not friends anymore."

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.067
-I mean, we're talking, you know, we're going to --

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:29.067
-What a great game. What a great game that is.

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:31.400
-It's more frustrating than anything to be --

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.801
-I think it's a fantastic game.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.834
-I'm pretty sure I end every night more upset

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:38.067
after I play "Mario Party" with friends than -- than happy.

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:40.033
-No, that is not true. -Absolutely!

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:41.901
-No, you're psyched -- -You're stealing stars.

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.234
You're sucking coins, man.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.100
Your -- Your bo-- You know what I mean?

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.067
It's awful! -You're very young.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:49.000
I was gonna ask you, do you --

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.634
do you ever, like, wait in line for, like, a console or a game?

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:54.300
Like, 'cause I had to do that.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.834
-My parents would not let me stay out

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.067
for the "Halo 3" release.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:58.834
For -- For, like, the Xbox 360.

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:01.601
"Halo 3." Tyler -- I was, like, 14.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.100
I was too young, obviously. Midnight release.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.734
Because remember -- you remember midnight releases.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:06.267
-I d-- Of course I remember midnight releases.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:07.934
-I feel like they don't happen anymore. It's just --

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:09.434
-But you -- So you -- You were too young

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.100
and they go, "No, you're not -- Tyler, you're not getting it."

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.634
-So I'm 14. Jon's 18.

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:15.434
He goes and he stays out all night and gets the --

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.868
the midnight release copy.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.200
I'm staying up in my bed

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.267
just, like, waiting for him to come upstairs and --

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.567
-With it. -With the game and be like,

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:23.868
"Tyler, we're playing." -Yes.

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.400
-Because that was the whole plan, the whole strategy.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.901
My mom was like, "Tyler, you're not going."

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:28.400
And then Jon and I are like, "Alright, dude.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.968
Like, let me tell you what's gonna happen."

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.334
"You're gonna wake me up at midnight.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:32.601
-So you're already playing games.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.067
-"And we're gonna play the game." Yeah.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.534
We played -- We stayed up till 3:00 a.m.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:37.567
And we won every team doubles game that we played.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:40.234
-And so you're playing the game and then you go like,

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:43.601
"Oh, I think I could probably make a living off of this."

00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:45.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.767
And -- And how do you tell your mom

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.467
who just said you can't go out to the mall?

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.234
You're like, "Mom, this is my future.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.934
I'm actually -- I'm building a future

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.701
for our family right now." -Right.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.133
Yeah, "Listen, Mom..."

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:57.801
-You have a very cool mom. -That story is phenomenal.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:00.667
It was simple, you know? Money talks, right?

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.033
And...

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.367
-So you started making money. -Yeah.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.067
So once I started streaming, that was where I --

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.734
where I started making, like, a proper living,

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:09.133
and I started making -- I think when I started, it was,

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:12.968
like, $20,000, was the projected sales.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:15.901
-Wow.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.734
-And I finally, you know, started making, I think, like,

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.501
anywhere from, like, $30,000 to $40,000,

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:22.067
and I was also going to college full-time

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:24.667
and working a job at Noodles &amp; Company.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.634
And -- And I told -- You know, listen.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:30.267
-Wow. Noodles &amp; Company. -Phenomenal food, actually.

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:31.601
#NotAnAd.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.334
But seriously, yeah, I worked there for three years.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:36.300
And all of my focus was --

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.834
You know, no relationships, really.

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:39.734
Never really hung out with my friends either.

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:42.267
It was either I was streaming, going to school, or working.

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:44.234
And finally, I was like, "Mom, listen, if I make more than,

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:45.701
you know, minimum wage, I'm like --

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.067
I'm going to pursue this," right?

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:48.467
I'm going to go full-time, right?

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:49.934
Because I'm only doing, you know --

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.434
-But what if you don't make enough money?

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.033
-I told her immediately. I made a promise

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.434
with both my wife, Jess, and my mom.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:55.868
I was like -- And my brothers and --

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.300
-Your girlfriend, Jess, at the time.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.667
-Girlfriend Jess at the time.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.934
Because, you know, she was also super skeptical of, like --

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.667
just the longevity of the whole thing.

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:05.501
You know what I mean? Like, you -- you don't know.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.100
-Yeah. -I wasn't making millions.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.100
-This is not an occupation... -100%. It was not.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.734
-...that we grew up with -- -It was --

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:12.434
Yeah, it was like free agency is what it felt like.

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:15.000
I mean, it could have just collapsed at any moment.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.067
And...

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.567
Like, "I'll go back to college if I ever, you know,

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:22.100
start making less than what I was making when I started."

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.601
-You're doing a thing. You're helping --

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.734
You're having people take time-outs off their screens.

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:28.367
Can you explain what you're doing?

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:30.367
-Absolutely, man. Yeah, so we know --

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.467
Dude, I -- I've been gaming and --

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.701
and had a screen in front of my face,

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.834
you know, honestly, as long as I can remember.

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:38.868
Not, like, iPads because those didn't exist when I was a kid.

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:40.767
But, you know, I gamed so much, and when I streamed

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:42.167
and when I was grinding at the time,

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:46.067
I was doing, like, 18-hour days, was how long I would stream for.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:47.601
-Geez. -Dude.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.701
And I wish older me would have been able to tell younger me,

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:52.100
"You know, you can take a day off or even, you know,

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:57.100
even an hour off and just relax, spend time with family,

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.868
and just kind of, you know, again, take time out of --

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:02.400
off the screen and of gaming."

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.801
And that's what I've been doing a lot now.

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:06.334
And it's -- -Who are you partnering with?

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:07.868
-Oh, dude, we're partnering with Thrive Global

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:10.667
and the Center for Scholars &amp; Storytellers.

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:12.400
And we have -- You know,

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.968
we're just preaching, you know, again, take time-outs.

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:17.100
So for me, personally, one of my two favorite things

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.033
that I love to do -- I'm going on daily walks,

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:22.067
whether it be at a gym, or after,

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:23.434
and just, you know, pet time.

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:25.000
I have three amazing, beautiful dogs.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.434
Dude, we love them so much.

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:28.567
-Dude, I know you. You're on the incline.

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:29.868
3.5. -3.5, man.

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:32.200
3.58-degree incline is where we're starting.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.167
-That's my man right there. That's Tyler "Ninja" Blevins.

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:37.300
It's always good to see you, buddy.

